==Dutch==

===Etymology===
Originally the dative and accusative form of {{m|nl|jij}}/{{m|nl|gij}}, from {{inh|nl|dum|u}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|iu}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*iwwiz}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*iwwiz}}, {{der|nl|gmw|-}} variant of {{m|gem-pro|*izwiz}}, dative/accusative of {{m|gem-pro|*jūz}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*yúHs}}. {{doublet|nl|jou}}.

The use as a nominative form is linked to the polite address {{m|nl|uwe edelheid||your nobility, your gentility}}, which was shortened to {{m|nl|U E.}} in writing and at times accordingly pronounced {{IPAfont|/yˈ(w)eː/}}. It is debated, however, whether this was the actual cause of the development or whether it merely reinforced it. Compare {{m+|en|you}}, which was originally an object form, as well as {{cog|af|ons}} and nonstandard {{m+|nl|hun}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fy|jo}}, {{cog|nds|jo}}, {{m|nds|ju}}, {{cog|en|you}}, {{cog|de|euch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|nl|Nl-u.ogg}}
* {{IPA|nl|/y/}}

